"assessment_outcome": "may_meet_conditional_standard",
"explanation": "The patient has experienced a single blackout of undetermined nature. Verified facts confirm the mechanism is undetermined after investigation and there have been no further events for 5 years. According to guideline evidence, a person with a single blackout of undetermined nature should not drive for 5 years. However, since exactly 5 event-free years have elapsed and appropriate specialist information is available, the patient meets the prerequisite criterion for a conditional licence consideration (no further blackouts for at least 5 years). The absence of diabetes, visual defects, diplopia, or monocular vision issues does not negate this finding but confirms other modules are not restricting eligibility. An established restriction regarding the 'undetermined' nature remains relevant to the conditional pathway; however, the time criterion is satisfied.",
